---
import GuideLayout from "../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro";
import { getGuide } from "../../data/guides";

const guide = getGuide("website-development-cost-india");

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "What is the cheapest way to get a business website in India?",
    a: "The cheapest option is a DIY website builder, which costs roughly ₹3,000–₹15,000 per year including a domain and plan. A professionally built simple business website typically starts around ₹15,000 and gives you better speed, SEO and ownership of the code.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is ₹10,000 enough for a website?",
    a: "₹10,000 can cover a basic one-page or template-based website, but it rarely includes custom design, SEO setup, content writing or ongoing support. For most businesses, a budget of ₹25,000–₹60,000 produces a website that actually generates enquiries.",
  },
  {
    q: "Are there hidden costs after a website is built?",
    a: "The main recurring costs are the domain (about ₹800–₹1,500 per year), hosting (₹0–₹15,000 per year), premium plugins or themes if used, and optional maintenance (₹2,000–₹15,000 per month). Always ask for these in writing before you start.",
  },
  {
    q: "Should I pay a website developer upfront?",
    a: "A common and fair structure is 30–50% upfront, a milestone payment after design approval, and the balance at launch. Avoid paying 100% upfront, and make sure the contract states that you own the code, domain and content.",
  },
];
---

<GuideLayout guide={guide} faqs={faqs}>
  <p>
    "How much does a website cost?" is the first question almost every business owner asks — and the
    answers online range from ₹5,000 to ₹50 lakh. This guide breaks down realistic 2026 website
    development costs in India by type of website, explains what drives the price up or down, and
    shows you how to budget for the running costs most quotes leave out.
  </p>

  <h2>Website cost in India by type (2026)</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Type of website</th><th>Typical cost (INR)</th><th>Timeline</th><th>Best for</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Simple business website (5–7 pages)</td><td>₹15,000 – ₹50,000</td><td>1–3 weeks</td><td>Local businesses, clinics, consultants, freelancers</td></tr>
        <tr><td>CMS business website (10–30 pages, blog)</td><td>₹40,000 – ₹1,50,000</td><td>3–6 weeks</td><td>Growing SMBs that publish content and need SEO</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Landing page (single, conversion-focused)</td><td>₹8,000 – ₹40,000</td><td>1–2 weeks</td><td>Ad campaigns, product launches, events</td></tr>
        <tr><td>E-commerce store (Shopify / WooCommerce)</td><td>₹75,000 – ₹2,50,000</td><td>3–6 weeks</td><td>D2C brands and retailers going online</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Custom e-commerce platform</td><td>₹3,00,000 – ₹10,00,000+</td><td>8–16 weeks</td><td>Large catalogues, multi-vendor, custom logic</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Custom web application / portal</td><td>₹2,00,000 – ₹15,00,000+</td><td>6–16 weeks</td><td>SaaS, booking systems, dashboards, internal tools</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="note">
    These are typical market ranges for professional agencies in India. Freelancers may be cheaper;
    large enterprise agencies can be significantly more expensive. The only way to get an exact number
    is a written, itemised quote for your specific scope.
  </p>

  <h2>What affects the cost of a website?</h2>
  <h3>1. Number of unique page designs</h3>
  <p>
    Ten pages that share one layout cost far less than ten pages that each need a custom design.
    Most small-business sites need only 3–5 unique templates.
  </p>
  <h3>2. Custom features and integrations</h3>
  <p>
    Booking calendars, payment gateways (Razorpay, Stripe, UPI), user logins, CRM connections, multi-language
    support and AI chatbots each add development and testing time.
  </p>
  <h3>3. Template vs. custom design</h3>
  <p>
    A customised template is faster and cheaper. A fully custom design costs more but makes your brand
    stand out and is usually faster-loading because there is no unused template code.
  </p>
  <h3>4. Content creation</h3>
  <p>
    Copywriting, product photography and product data entry are often the hidden budget items. If you
    provide finished text and images, costs drop noticeably.
  </p>
  <h3>5. SEO and performance</h3>
  <p>
    A website that isn't found on Google is a brochure nobody reads. Technical SEO — fast load times,
    structured data, a sitemap, clean URLs and Search Console setup — should be included in any
    professional build, not sold later as an extra.
  </p>

  <h2>Ongoing yearly costs</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Typical cost</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Domain name (.com / .in)</td><td>₹800 – ₹1,500 per year</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Hosting</td><td>₹0 (static sites on free CDNs) – ₹15,000 per year</td></tr>
        <tr><td>SSL certificate</td><td>Usually free (Let's Encrypt / host-provided)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Business email</td><td>₹1,500 – ₹2,500 per user per year</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Maintenance &amp; updates</td><td>₹2,000 – ₹15,000 per month (optional)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>DIY website builder vs. hiring a developer</h2>
  <p>
    Builders such as Wix or Squarespace are fine for a very simple online presence. You'll outgrow them
    if you need strong SEO, fast performance, custom features, or full ownership of your site. A
    professional developer costs more upfront but typically delivers a faster, better-ranking website you
    fully own.
  </p>

  <h2>How to get an accurate website quote</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Write down the goal of the website (calls, bookings, online sales, credibility).</li>
    <li>List the pages you need and 2–3 websites you like.</li>
    <li>Note any features: payments, booking, login, blog, multiple languages.</li>
    <li>Ask for a fixed, itemised quote that includes design, development, SEO setup, hosting and launch.</li>
    <li>Confirm in writing that you will own the code, domain and content.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Want a number for your project? <a href="/contact/">Contact KYK AstroTech</a> for a free consultation
    and a fixed quote, or read about our <a href="/services/web-development/">website development services</a> and <a href="/services/ecommerce-development/">e-commerce development</a>.
  </p>
</GuideLayout>
